{"chunk_id": "4be2401a23dc", "text": "Arjuna battles the aged king Bhagadatta, who fights from his massive war elephant and showers Arjuna and Krishna with weapons. Arjuna skillfully destroys Bhagadatta\u2019s bow, armor, and missiles, wounding the elephant and pressing the attack. In desperation, Bhagadatta invokes the infallible Vaishnava weapon and hurls it at Arjuna, but Krishna steps in front of the hero and receives it on his own chest, where it harmlessly turns into a garland. Arjuna questions why Krishna broke his vow not to fight, and Krishna reveals the ancient origin of the weapon, once granted to Naraka and passed down to Bhagadatta. With the threat removed, Arjuna kills the elephant and then Bhagadatta. The episode highlights Krishna\u2019s divine nature and protective role, while confirming Arjuna as the decisive warrior on the battlefield.\nArjuna kills Bhagadatta after Krishna absorbs the Vaishnava weapon, then continues battling Gandhara princes Vrishaka and Achala.\nThemes: divine intervention, heroic duel, invincible weapon, battlefield valor, fate and boon", "vector": [-0.0031991261057555676, -0.009351548738777637, -0.0041607036255300045, 0.026743557304143906, 0.0009908427018672228, 0.012355014681816101, -0.027693428099155426, -0.015251453034579754, -0.029405871406197548, -0.015358480624854565, 0.02040216326713562, -0.0022525994572788477, 0.0021171425469219685, -0.01086331531405449, -0.0017241500318050385, 0.004719254560768604, 0.05067763477563858, -0.010803112760186195, 0.02135203406214714, -0.017753226682543755, -0.003963370807468891, 0.005966796539723873, -0.0025887335650622845, 0.01660267822444439, -0.005003546830266714, 0.024509351700544357, 0.007391603197902441, -0.023198261857032776, 0.0034315770026296377, -0.013739686459302902, -0.009211074560880661, 0.003165679983794689, -0.003271035384386778, -0.00034533170401118696, -0.03633591905236244, -0.010816491208970547, -0.002777704270556569, -0.015278209932148457, 0.011933593079447746, 0.009625